    "EM20",
    "Mercato EM20",
    "MEI EM20 energy meter",
    "Mercato Automacao EM20"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Mercato MEI-EM20 three-phase sub-metering energy meter with temperature, pulse and analog I/O.",
  "summary": "The MEI-EM20 is a three-phase sub-meter that speaks BACnet IP, BACnet Ethernet and BACnet MS/TP (on its RS-485 port) at the same time as Modbus and SNMP. Volts, currents, power, power factor, energy, pulse totals and min / max peaks are Analog Values; the five NTC inputs and the 0-10 V / 4-20 mA input are Analog Inputs; the two relays and the 0-10 V output can be driven over the network. Built-in trend logs keep about 60 days of hourly energy data.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet Ethernet",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "From table 3 of the user manual (REV K). The device object (named MEI-EM20) is not repeated in the points list.",
    "The table has no access column. Outputs (AO 1, BO 1-2) are listed as commandable and the reset BVs, schedules, calendar and notification class as writable; everything else as read-only.",
    "AV 49 and AV 50 are both printed as \"BC voltage min\"; AV 50 is the BC voltage maximum per its description. Names are kept as printed.",
    "Pulse accumulator and pulse trend units are set by the user (\"User cfg\"). NTC input units follow the meter temperature setting.",
    "Object names change with the meter language setting; these are the English names."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "MEI EM20 - User's manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "REV K (2021-03-22)",
    "url": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0486/4104/8742/files/Manual_Integrador_-_MEI-EM20.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set a unique device ID first (the default 4194303 means unconfigured and the meter ignores Who-Is), then read total power, energy and the per-phase values. Relays and the analog output can be commanded from the BMS when their function is set to network control.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 1",
        "name": "DO_1",
        "why": "Relay output 1 command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 2",
        "name": "DO_2",
        "why": "Relay output 2 command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 19",
        "name": "Total active power",
        "why": "Total active power, kW"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 27",
        "name": "Imported active energy",
        "why": "Imported active energy, kWh"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 28",
        "name": "Exported active energy",
        "why": "Exported active energy, kWh"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 25",
        "name": "Total PF",
        "why": "Total power factor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "A voltage",
        "why": "Phase A voltage"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 7",
        "name": "A current",
        "why": "Phase A current"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 26",
        "name": "Frequency",
        "why": "Line frequency"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Each relay output must be configured with no internal function (not schedule-driven) before BACnet or Modbus can control it.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device ID range 0-4194302, shared by all BACnet datalinks; the factory value 4194303 means unconfigured and the meter does not answer Who-Is.",
      "BACnet IP uses UDP 47808 by default; BACnet Ethernet uses the factory MAC address.",
      "BACnet MS/TP runs on the isolated RS-485 port (shared with Modbus RTU; one protocol at a time). Set station address and max master (default 127).",
      "Avoid enabling two BACnet datalinks to the same network; it can create a loop."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Writing 1 to BV 1 / BV 2 / BV 3 clears energy totals, pulse totals or min/max peaks; do not write them cyclically.",
      "Writing 0 to a trend log Record_Count erases that log.",
      "Trend log timestamps mark the end of each hour or interval."
    ]
  },
